---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is chilli powder?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Chilli powder is dried chilli ground to a fine 60–80 mesh. It delivers uniform, blendable heat — typically 20,000–50,000 SHU — for hot sauces, seasoning and industrial food. Heat, colour and flavour vary independently, so a specification names the variety and SHU window, not a generic 'chilli powder'."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What mesh size is chilli powder?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Standard chilli powder is 60–80 mesh — fine enough for even dispersion and smooth mouthfeel. Coarser (20–40) is for flakes; finer (100+) for smooth sauces. Mesh is adjustable to your requirement."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which variety should I use for chilli powder?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Sanying (Tianying), Zidantou and Seven-Star (20,000–50,000 SHU) are the workhorses for hot sauce and seasoning. For extra heat, Jixin and Xiaomi exceed 50,000 SHU. Name the variety and a precise SHU window for batch-to-batch consistency."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Chilli Powder (60–80 Mesh) | Tenda Peppers"
  description="China chilli powder manufacturer — 60–80 mesh, 20,000–50,000 SHU, from Sanying, Zidantou and Seven-Star for hot sauce, seasoning and industrial food. ISO 9001 & HACCP."
  jsonLd={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <div class="container section">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#6b5a54;margin-bottom:16px;">
      <a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/products/dried-chillies/">Dried Chillies</a> &rsaquo; Chilli Powder
    </nav>
    <h1>Chilli Powder (60–80 Mesh)</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Finely ground dried chilli — 60–80 mesh, 20,000–50,000 SHU — the workhorse for hot sauces,
      seasoning and industrial food, milled from Sanying, Zidantou and Seven-Star.
    </p>

    <div class="takeaways">
      <strong>Short answer:</strong> Chilli powder is dried chilli ground to 60–80 mesh for uniform, blendable heat — the default form for hot sauces and industrial food. It is specified by variety (or a precise SHU window), because heat, colour and flavour vary independently; ordering generic &ldquo;chilli powder&rdquo; is how batch-to-batch inconsistency happens.
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What is chilli powder?</h2>
    <p>
      Chilli powder is dried chilli ground to a fine 60–80 mesh for uniform, blendable heat. Unlike
      flakes or whole chillies, it disperses evenly through a sauce or seasoning, which is why it is
      the default form for hot sauces, snack seasoning and industrial food. Heat, colour and flavour
      vary independently, so the right way to order is by variety and SHU window — see our
      <a href="/blog/how-to-specify-chilli-powder/">how to specify chilli powder</a> guide.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Variety</th><th>Heat (SHU)</th><th>Region</th><th>Best for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Sanying / Tianying</strong></td><td>20,000 – 50,000</td><td>Henan, Hebei</td><td>Hot sauce, chilli oil</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Zidantou (bullet)</strong></td><td>20,000 – 50,000</td><td>Shandong, Anhui</td><td>Hot sauce, industrial</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Seven-Star</strong></td><td>20,000 – 50,000</td><td>Shandong, Shanxi</td><td>Snack seasoning, hot-pot</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What is chilli powder used for?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Hot sauces and chilli oil</li>
      <li>Snack and instant-noodle seasoning</li>
      <li>Seasoning blends and spice mixes</li>
      <li>Industrial food and processed seasoning</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">How to specify chilli powder</h2>
    <p>
      Name five things: the variety (or SHU window), heat in SHU, mesh, moisture and colour (ASTA) if
      relevant. For hot sauce, Sanying and Zidantou are the classic pair; Seven-Star suits snack
      seasoning. Heat is non-linear, so a precise window — not "hot" or "medium" — is what keeps your
      product consistent batch to batch.
    </p>
    <p class="data-note">
      Heat values are representative per variety. Confirm your exact SHU window, mesh and moisture
      when you inquire.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What is chilli powder?</h3>
      <p>Chilli powder is dried chilli ground to a fine 60–80 mesh. It delivers uniform, blendable heat — typically 20,000–50,000 SHU — for hot sauces, seasoning and industrial food. Heat, colour and flavour vary independently, so a specification names the variety and SHU window, not a generic 'chilli powder'.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What mesh size is chilli powder?</h3>
      <p>Standard chilli powder is 60–80 mesh — fine enough for even dispersion and smooth mouthfeel. Coarser (20–40) is for flakes; finer (100+) for smooth sauces. Mesh is adjustable to your requirement.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Which variety should I use for chilli powder?</h3>
      <p>Sanying (Tianying), Zidantou and Seven-Star (20,000–50,000 SHU) are the workhorses for hot sauce and seasoning. For extra heat, Jixin and Xiaomi exceed 50,000 SHU. Name the variety and a precise SHU window for batch-to-batch consistency.</p>
    </div>

